 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DfS8Uu4HzN1/",
 "title": "Email Marketing and AI Summaries",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "The creator explains how AI email summaries will impact marketing in the next 12 months. He advises marketers to ditch cheesy openings and include action, product, and deadlines in the first 150 to 200 characters.",
 "key_points": [
  "AI is now summarizing emails before people open them.",
  "Live text in emails dictates what shows up in AI summaries.",
  "AI summaries cannot pull words that are baked into an image.",
  "AI summaries look at the first 150 to 200 characters of your email.",
  "Do not use cheesy openers; instead, start with action, product, and deadline."
 ],
 "content": "Your email's first 200 characters just got WAY more important. AI is summarizing emails before people even open them. You need to ditch the cheesy intro and get straight to the action, product, or deadline. Oh, and make sure your text isn't trapped inside an image!! Comment EMAIL to grab the link to my marketing podcast. So there's something going on that will change all of our marketing, I don't care if you're a B2B, B2C marketer, doesn't matter what you are, in the next 12 months. And that is something called live text. So, when you get an email, there are now AI summaries. The AI is looking in the email saying what's in there. What you put in live text—I'm going to tell you exactly what live text is—is going to dictate what shows up in those summaries. If you can highlight the text in the email, that's live text. If you have important things in your email and the words are baked into an image, the AI summaries cannot pull out any words that are in an image. The most important thing you can start to think about is what are you going to do to have the most important parts of your email show up in these AI summaries, because if you don't, your email marketing is going to be screwed. So what the AI summary is looking for, it's looking at the first 150 to 200 characters of your email. So in those first 150 to 200 characters, you can't do some sort of cheesy open, nobody cares, including you. What we do care about though is action plus product plus deadline. Register for the 2027 HR Compliance Briefing by Friday deadline. This is what you need to be doing in the first 200 characters, because that's what the AI summaries are looking for.",
 "status": "done",
